Expand and simplify completely: \begin{align*}
x\left(x(1+x)+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*}

negative:
To expand and simplify the given expression, we'll follow the order of operations (PEMDAS):

\begin{align*}
x\left(x(1+x)+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*}

First, distribute the x inside the parentheses:

\begin{align*}
x\left(x+x^2+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*}

Combine like terms inside the parentheses:

\begin{align*}
x\left(3x^2+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*}

Distribute the x outside the parentheses:

\begin{align*}
3x^3+2x^2-3x^2+3x-6
\end{align*}

Combine like terms:

\begin{align*}
3x^3- x^2+3x-6
\end{align*}

The simplified expression is:

\boxed{3x^3 - x^2 + 3x - 6}

